WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:20.950
Cheetah presents Halloween Horror by Gina D. B. Clement.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.950
Chapter 1 Salem

00:26.000 --> 00:30.950
Salem is a beautiful American town in Massachusetts, USA.

00:31.000 --> 00:35.950
Naum Keog, city of peace, is its Indian name.

00:36.000 --> 00:42.950
But it is also called the Witch City, because of the witch hangings of 1692.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.950
There are seven historical witch museums in Salem.

00:48.000 --> 00:54.950
They all have a lot of information on the witches and hangings of 1692.

00:55.000 --> 00:59.950
Kelly and Meghan Connor are two sisters.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.950
They come from San Francisco, California.

01:03.000 --> 01:10.950
The Connor family now lives in Salem, because Mr. Connor teaches French at the University of Boston.

01:11.000 --> 01:15.950
Kelly is 14, and Meghan is 13.

01:16.000 --> 01:19.950
They go to Salem Middle School, and they like it.

01:20.000 --> 01:22.950
Kelly has red hair and blue eyes.

01:23.000 --> 01:26.950
She's tall and plays basketball for the school team.

01:27.000 --> 01:29.950
Meghan has fair hair and blue eyes.

01:30.000 --> 01:32.950
She's a champion swimmer.

01:33.000 --> 01:35.950
She is a member of the Salem Swimming Team.

01:36.000 --> 01:42.950
It's Friday, October 28, and Halloween is on Monday, October 31.

01:43.000 --> 01:47.950
Kelly and Meghan are very excited, because they love Halloween.

01:48.000 --> 01:52.950
This is their first Halloween in Salem, the Witch City.

01:53.000 --> 01:55.950
I think about Halloween all the time. Says Meghan.

01:56.000 --> 01:58.950
Me too. Says Kelly.

01:59.000 --> 02:03.950
We must buy a pumpkin and make a jack-o'-lantern. Says their mother.

02:04.000 --> 02:10.950
Now finish your breakfast. It's late. School starts in 20 minutes.

02:11.000 --> 02:14.950
The girls eat their eggs and drink their milk.

02:15.000 --> 02:17.950
Then they go upstairs to brush their teeth.

02:18.000 --> 02:20.950
They're ready at quarter past eight.

02:21.000 --> 02:24.950
Goodbye, Mom. Don't forget to buy the pumpkin.

02:25.000 --> 02:28.950
Okay, goodbye, girls.

02:29.000 --> 02:32.950
Kelly and Meghan always walk to school.

02:33.000 --> 02:39.950
They meet their friends, Susan Garcia, Nick Lee, and Bill Goldberg.

02:40.000 --> 02:45.950
I'm so excited about Halloween. Says Susan. Susan is Hispanic American.

02:46.000 --> 02:49.950
She is 13 years old and has long black hair.

02:50.000 --> 02:53.950
This is the first time we can have a party without our parents.

02:54.000 --> 02:58.950
We must find a place to have the party.

02:59.000 --> 03:02.950
Says Nick. He is 14 years old, and he's a good cook.

03:03.000 --> 03:05.950
His parents have a Chinese restaurant in Salem.

03:06.000 --> 03:09.950
Let's see. Says Bill, I can ask my grandmother.

03:10.000 --> 03:13.950
Bill Goldberg is a handsome boy of 14.

03:14.000 --> 03:16.950
His favorite school subject is science.

03:17.000 --> 03:18.950
He lives with his grandmother.

03:19.000 --> 03:23.950
Susan, do you have a scary costume for Halloween? Asks Kelly.

03:24.000 --> 03:27.950
It's a surprise. I can't tell you. Says Susan.

03:28.000 --> 03:29.950
Do you believe in ghosts?

03:30.000 --> 03:30.950
Bill asks.

03:31.000 --> 03:31.950
Yes.

03:32.000 --> 03:32.950
They all say.

03:33.000 --> 03:34.950
Oh, I don't.

03:35.000 --> 03:37.950
Bill, science can explain everything.

03:38.000 --> 03:39.950
Really? Says Nick.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.950
A lot of strange things happen on Halloween night.

03:43.000 --> 03:44.950
My grandparents come from China.

03:45.000 --> 03:48.950
They believe in ghosts and evil spirits, too.

03:49.000 --> 03:50.950
Bill laughs.

03:51.000 --> 03:54.950
Do you remember the story of the old woman in the cemetery?

03:55.000 --> 03:59.950
Oh, Nick. Please don't tell us again. Says Bill.

04:00.000 --> 04:01.950
Nick smiles mysteriously.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.950
It's 8.30 a.m.

04:04.000 --> 04:07.000
and the school bell is ringing.

04:17.000 --> 04:17.950
Chapter Two.

04:18.000 --> 04:21.000
The Witch Museum.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.950
School finishes at 3.30 p.m.

04:29.000 --> 04:32.950
Kelly and Megan meet their friends outside.

04:33.000 --> 04:35.950
Do you have any ideas for our Halloween party?

04:36.000 --> 04:36.950
Kelly asks.

04:37.000 --> 04:38.950
No, I don't. Says Susan.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.950
I have an idea. Says Megan.

04:42.000 --> 04:43.950
Let's visit one of the Salem Witch Museums.

04:44.000 --> 04:46.950
We can get many ideas from there.

04:47.000 --> 04:49.950
That's a good idea. Says Susan.

04:50.000 --> 04:52.950
There are a lot of scary things there.

04:53.000 --> 04:56.950
Remember, Salem is the Witch City.

04:57.000 --> 05:00.950
At the museum, there are pictures of the witch hangings.

05:01.000 --> 05:04.950
There are also the names of the Salem Witches of 1692.

05:05.000 --> 05:08.950
We can read about their terrible magic.

05:09.000 --> 05:10.950
Oh, how exciting!

05:11.000 --> 05:12.950
Oh, how exciting! Say Megan and Kelly.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.950
Let's go. Says Susan.

05:16.000 --> 05:17.950
The girls call Nick and Bill.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.950
Together, the five friends go to the museum.

05:21.000 --> 05:23.950
When they arrive, it's late.

05:24.000 --> 05:26.950
How many tickets do you want? Asks the attendant.

05:27.000 --> 05:29.950
Five tickets, please. Says Bill.

05:30.000 --> 05:31.950
That's $10.

05:32.000 --> 05:34.950
Remember, the museum closes at 5 p.m.

05:35.000 --> 05:36.950
You only have half an hour.

05:37.000 --> 05:39.950
The five friends walk around the museum.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.950
They look at the interesting exhibits.

05:43.000 --> 05:47.950
Look, here are the names of the Witches of 1692.

05:48.000 --> 05:51.950
And here are the pictures of the hangings. Says Nick.

05:52.000 --> 05:53.950
Look at this rope, says Bill.

05:54.000 --> 05:57.950
How scary! Say the girls.

05:58.000 --> 05:59.950
I'm going upstairs. Says Megan.

06:00.000 --> 06:01.950
Be careful. Says Kelly.

06:02.000 --> 06:02.950
Megan laughs.

06:03.000 --> 06:06.000
I'm not afraid of witches or ghosts.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.950
There are no visitors upstairs.

06:15.000 --> 06:18.950
There is a sweet smell of roses in the air.

06:19.000 --> 06:21.950
Megan walks around and looks at everything.

06:22.000 --> 06:24.950
Then she sees an old lady.

06:25.000 --> 06:29.950
She has a long black dress with small black buttons.

06:30.000 --> 06:34.950
Her skin is very white and her lips are very red.

06:35.000 --> 06:38.950
There is a strange red mark around her neck.

06:39.000 --> 06:40.950
She smiles at Megan.

06:41.000 --> 06:45.950
Megan smiles too, but she is nervous.

06:46.000 --> 06:48.950
Suddenly the air is very cold.

06:49.000 --> 06:50.950
How strange!

06:51.000 --> 06:51.950
She thinks.

06:52.000 --> 06:55.000
I want to go downstairs.

07:03.000 --> 07:05.950
When Kelly sees her, she asks.

07:06.000 --> 07:06.950
What's upstairs?

07:07.000 --> 07:10.950
Oh, some interesting exhibits. Answers, Megan.

07:11.000 --> 07:16.950
The museum closes in five minutes. Says the attendant.

07:17.000 --> 07:22.950
Susan buys a book called Salem and the Witches of 1692.

07:23.000 --> 07:26.950
The three girls walk to the front door.

07:27.000 --> 07:30.950
Is there anyone still upstairs? Ask the attendant.

07:31.000 --> 07:32.950
Yes. Says Megan.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.950
There's an old lady.

07:35.000 --> 07:36.950
Really? Says the attendant.

07:37.000 --> 07:37.950
That's strange.

07:38.000 --> 07:41.950
You are the only visitors in the museum this afternoon.

07:42.000 --> 07:44.950
There aren't many visitors here on Fridays.

07:45.000 --> 07:48.950
There is an old lady upstairs. Says Megan.

07:49.000 --> 07:52.950
I'm going upstairs to see. Says the attendant.

07:53.000 --> 07:55.950
After a few minutes he returns.

07:56.000 --> 07:58.950
His face is red and he says.

07:59.000 --> 07:59.950
Is this a joke?

08:00.000 --> 08:01.950
There's no one upstairs.

08:02.000 --> 08:06.950
And the only door of the museum is this front door.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.950
Megan's friends look at her.

08:09.000 --> 08:10.950
She is silent.

08:11.000 --> 08:12.950
Then she says.

08:13.000 --> 08:14.950
Let's look outside.

08:15.000 --> 08:18.950
They run out of the museum and look outside.

08:19.000 --> 08:20.950
There's no one in the street.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.950
Only a black cat.

08:24.000 --> 08:30.950
After this strange experience they walk home.

08:31.000 --> 08:35.950
Now I have a lot of ideas for a Halloween party. Says Kelly.

08:36.000 --> 08:38.950
Yes, I do too. Says Susan.

08:39.000 --> 08:41.950
Very quiet, Megan. Says Bill.

08:42.000 --> 08:45.000
I'm thinking about the old lady at the museum.

08:56.000 --> 08:56.950
Hello.

08:57.000 --> 08:58.950
Is the museum still open?

08:59.000 --> 09:00.950
Yes, it is.

09:01.000 --> 09:02.950
Five tickets, please.

09:03.000 --> 09:03.950
Are you students?

09:04.000 --> 09:05.950
Yes, we are.

09:06.000 --> 09:07.950
Then you have a special price.

09:08.000 --> 09:09.950
It's ten dollars for each student.

09:10.000 --> 09:11.950
Here you are.

09:12.000 --> 09:14.950
Do you have any information about the museum?

09:15.000 --> 09:18.950
Yes, there are some books near the window over there.

09:19.000 --> 09:21.950
What time does the museum close?

09:22.000 --> 09:23.950
It closes at five.

09:24.000 --> 09:31.950
The origins of Halloween.

09:32.000 --> 09:33.950
Date.

09:34.000 --> 09:35.950
Twenty-two A.D.

09:36.000 --> 09:36.950
Place.

09:37.000 --> 09:38.950
British Isles.

09:39.000 --> 09:39.950
Hello.

09:40.000 --> 09:41.950
My name is Brennis.

09:42.000 --> 09:44.950
I'm a Selt and a Pagan.

09:45.000 --> 09:48.950
Let me tell you about an important Celtic festival.

09:49.000 --> 09:56.950
Samhain is the last day of summer and the last day of the Celtic year, October 31st.

09:57.000 --> 10:00.950
Samhain is the Celtic god of death.

10:01.000 --> 10:03.950
We are all afraid of him.

10:04.000 --> 10:09.950
On October 31st, we dress as witches, ghosts, and skeletons.

10:10.000 --> 10:12.950
We make fires to scare the evil spirits.

10:13.000 --> 10:16.950
We also play games to bring good luck in the new year.

10:17.000 --> 10:27.950
Oh, and the apples we eat are for good luck too.

10:28.000 --> 10:29.950
Chapter 3.

10:30.000 --> 10:35.950
September 22nd, 1692.

10:36.000 --> 10:38.950
There is no school on Saturday.

10:39.000 --> 10:42.000
It is a cloudy autumn day.

10:43.000 --> 10:46.950
Autumn is usually a beautiful season in Salem.

10:47.000 --> 10:51.950
The leaves on the trees are yellow, red, and orange.

10:52.000 --> 10:56.950
Mr. and Mrs. Connor have a big orange pumpkin.

10:57.000 --> 10:59.950
They are making a jack-o-lantern.

11:00.000 --> 11:04.950
When it's finished, we can put it in front of the window. Says Mr. Connor.

11:05.000 --> 11:07.950
Are you girls ready for Halloween?

11:08.000 --> 11:08.950
No, Dad.

11:09.000 --> 11:11.950
We must find a place for the party. Says Kelly.

11:12.000 --> 11:14.950
We must make our costumes too. Says Megan.

11:15.000 --> 11:19.950
Today is a perfect day to do many things. Says Mrs. Connor.

11:20.000 --> 11:21.950
Finish your homework this morning.

11:22.000 --> 11:24.950
Then you can look for a place for the party this afternoon.

11:25.000 --> 11:28.950
I can start my science homework. Says Megan.

11:29.000 --> 11:31.950
I'm a study English. Says Kelly.

11:32.000 --> 11:33.950
I have a test on Wednesday.

11:34.000 --> 11:38.000
They go to their room and study until noon.

11:39.000 --> 11:41.000
Then the phone rings.

11:47.000 --> 11:47.950
Hello.

11:48.000 --> 11:48.950
This is Bill.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.950
I have a place for our party.

11:51.000 --> 11:51.950
Really?

11:52.000 --> 11:52.950
That's great.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.950
Where is it? Says Kelly.

11:55.000 --> 11:56.950
It's a surprise.

11:57.000 --> 11:59.950
Meet me and Nick in front of the school at 1.30pm.

12:00.000 --> 12:01.950
We can go together.

12:02.000 --> 12:02.950
Okay.

12:03.000 --> 12:05.000
At half past one then. Says Kelly.

12:08.000 --> 12:10.950
The five friends meet in front of their school.

12:11.000 --> 12:12.950
They are very excited.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.950
Where is the place? Ask Susan.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.950
Follow me, says Bill.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.950
My grandmother knows this place.

12:19.000 --> 12:22.950
It is the best place for a spooky Halloween party.

12:23.000 --> 12:24.950
They walk past the park.

12:25.000 --> 12:27.950
Past the tennis courts and past the church.

12:28.000 --> 12:30.950
Then they walk down a country road.

12:31.000 --> 12:34.950
At the end of the road they see an old cemetery.

12:35.000 --> 12:38.950
This is the oldest cemetery in Salem. Says Bill.

12:39.000 --> 12:41.950
They enter the old cemetery.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.950
Look at the dates on the tombstones.

12:44.000 --> 12:49.950
This one says September 22, 1692. Says Megan.

12:50.000 --> 12:55.950
This one says September 22, 1692, too. Says Kelly.

12:56.000 --> 12:58.950
Here's another tombstone with the same date.

12:59.000 --> 13:02.950
September 22, 1692. Says Nick.

13:03.000 --> 13:05.950
They look at a lot of tombstones.

13:06.000 --> 13:10.950
These are probably the tombstones of the Salem witches. Says Bill.

13:11.000 --> 13:11.950
How spooky.

13:12.000 --> 13:14.950
Let's go now. Says Susan.

13:15.000 --> 13:18.950
The five friends run to the country road.

13:19.000 --> 13:20.950
Then they walk for a few minutes.

13:21.000 --> 13:25.950
At the end of the road they see an old abandoned house.

13:26.000 --> 13:27.950
It is near a forest.

13:28.000 --> 13:31.950
There is a rose bush near the door.

13:32.000 --> 13:34.950
This is the house for our party. Says Bill.

13:35.000 --> 13:37.950
His friends are very surprised.

13:38.000 --> 13:39.950
They look at the house.

13:40.000 --> 13:40.950
Wow!

13:41.000 --> 13:42.950
Is this a haunted house?

13:43.000 --> 13:43.950
Nick asks.

13:44.000 --> 13:45.950
Bill laughs.

13:46.000 --> 13:48.950
This is a very old house.

13:49.000 --> 13:52.950
From the 1650s poor people sometimes live in it.

13:53.000 --> 13:54.950
But then they go away.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.950
It's abandoned.

13:57.000 --> 13:58.950
There is no electricity.

13:59.000 --> 14:01.950
Why is it abandoned? Asks Nick.

14:02.000 --> 14:04.950
They say strange things happen here.

14:05.000 --> 14:08.950
It's the perfect place for a spooky party.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.950
Remember, ghosts don't exist.

14:12.000 --> 14:12.950
Bill says.

14:13.000 --> 14:15.950
Are you sure? Asks Kelly.

14:16.000 --> 14:18.950
The five friends look at each other.

14:19.000 --> 14:22.950
There is something strange about this place. Says Nick.

14:23.000 --> 14:30.950
Chapter 4.

14:31.000 --> 14:33.950
The Abandoned House.

14:34.000 --> 14:42.950
Megan looks at the old house and says.

14:43.000 --> 14:45.950
Look at the writing above the door.

14:46.000 --> 14:49.950
Home of Abigail Cross.

14:50.000 --> 14:57.950
October 31st, 1627 to September 22nd, 1692.

14:58.000 --> 15:00.950
Who is Abigail Cross?

15:01.000 --> 15:02.950
Look at the date.

15:03.000 --> 15:06.950
September 22nd, 1692.

15:07.000 --> 15:09.950
Do you remember the tombstones?

15:10.000 --> 15:12.950
Many of them have the same date.

15:13.000 --> 15:15.950
You're right. Says Susan.

15:16.000 --> 15:21.950
Let me look in my new book, Salem and the Witches of 1692.

15:22.000 --> 15:24.950
After a few minutes, Susan says.

15:25.000 --> 15:26.950
Oh no!

15:27.000 --> 15:29.950
Abigail Cross is a witch.

15:30.000 --> 15:31.950
Her name is in this book.

15:32.000 --> 15:34.950
I don't like this old house.

15:35.000 --> 15:38.950
Let's find another place for the party. Says Kelly.

15:39.000 --> 15:40.950
You girls are silly.

15:41.000 --> 15:42.950
This is perfect. Says Bill.

15:43.000 --> 15:44.950
Come on, follow me.

15:45.000 --> 15:49.950
Bill is the first to enter the house.

15:50.000 --> 15:52.950
Nick and the girls follow.

15:53.000 --> 15:55.950
It is very cold inside.

15:56.000 --> 16:01.950
There is a big room with an old table, chairs and a cupboard.

16:02.000 --> 16:05.950
On the wall there is an old portrait of a woman.

16:06.000 --> 16:08.950
She is wearing a long black dress.

16:09.000 --> 16:11.950
She has a red rose in her hand.

16:12.000 --> 16:15.950
Her eyes are dark and evil.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.950
This portrait is very old.

16:19.000 --> 16:20.950
There's a date at the bottom.

16:21.000 --> 16:28.950
It says June 1659. Says Megan.

16:29.000 --> 16:32.950
It's probably a portrait of Abigail Cross. Says Nick.

16:33.000 --> 16:37.950
She's looking at us and she's smiling. Says Megan.

16:38.000 --> 16:41.950
What an evil smile. Says Susan.

16:42.000 --> 16:45.950
Everything here is so old and scary. Says Kelly.

16:46.000 --> 16:47.950
I like it. Says Nick.

16:48.000 --> 16:50.950
We can make spooky decorations and light candles.

16:51.000 --> 16:53.950
I can bring my portable radio for music.

16:54.000 --> 16:56.950
First we must clean this house.

16:57.000 --> 17:00.950
Then we can make the decorations. Says Susan.

17:01.000 --> 17:04.950
Nick and Bill go to buy some cleaning products.

17:05.000 --> 17:07.950
The girls talk about the party.

17:08.000 --> 17:10.950
How many chairs are there? Asks Kelly.

17:11.000 --> 17:13.950
There are eight chairs. Answers Megan.

17:14.000 --> 17:15.950
We must bring chairs from home.

17:16.000 --> 17:19.950
Fifteen of our friends are coming to the party. Says Susan.

17:20.000 --> 17:22.950
I want to look at the old kitchen.

17:23.000 --> 17:26.950
I want to look at the other rooms. Says Megan.

17:27.000 --> 17:31.950
She walks down a long corridor.

17:32.000 --> 17:36.950
She finds three rooms with some old furniture.

17:37.000 --> 17:43.950
Then she opens a small door and enters a dark bedroom.

17:44.000 --> 17:48.950
There is a sweet smell of roses.

17:49.000 --> 17:54.950
She sees a long black dress with small black buttons on a big bed.

17:55.000 --> 17:59.950
On the floor she sees a pair of old black boots.

18:00.000 --> 18:01.950
They are wet.

18:02.000 --> 18:04.950
She looks outside the window.

18:05.000 --> 18:06.950
It is raining.

18:07.000 --> 18:09.950
She looks in an old mirror.

18:10.000 --> 18:13.950
Someone in the mirror is looking at her.

18:14.000 --> 18:14.950
Megan is afraid.

18:15.000 --> 18:18.950
She wants to leave the room but her legs can't move.

18:19.000 --> 18:21.950
She wants to call Kelly and Susan.

18:22.000 --> 18:24.950
But she has no voice.

18:25.000 --> 18:27.950
Suddenly Kelly calls her.

18:28.000 --> 18:29.950
Megan, what are you doing?

18:30.000 --> 18:32.950
Megan can't answer.

18:33.000 --> 18:35.950
Kelly and Susan run to the bedroom.

18:36.000 --> 18:38.950
Megan, what's happening?

18:39.000 --> 18:40.950
Megan's face is white.

18:41.000 --> 18:44.950
She points to the black dress and the wet boots.

18:45.000 --> 18:47.950
The girls are very surprised.

18:48.000 --> 18:50.950
Do you remember the old lady at the museum?

18:51.000 --> 18:52.950
Megan whispers.

18:53.000 --> 18:56.950
This is her dress and those are her boots.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.950
Look, they're wet.

18:59.000 --> 19:01.950
Are you sure that old lady exists?

19:02.000 --> 19:04.950
It's your imagination. Says Kelly.

19:05.000 --> 19:06.950
Megan is angry.

19:07.000 --> 19:08.950
It's not my imagination.

19:09.000 --> 19:11.950
This is Abigail Cross's house.

19:12.000 --> 19:13.950
And these are her clothes.

19:14.000 --> 19:15.950
Abigail Cross is here.

19:16.000 --> 19:17.950
Abigail Cross is dead.

19:18.000 --> 19:20.000
But her ghost isn't.

19:26.000 --> 19:27.950
Chapter 5.

19:28.000 --> 19:30.000
Halloween Costumes.

19:33.000 --> 19:37.000
Megan, Kelly and Susan go back to the big room.

19:39.000 --> 19:40.950
They look at the old portrait.

19:41.000 --> 19:43.950
They don't like it.

19:44.000 --> 19:46.950
Soon the boys arrive with some cleaning products.

19:47.000 --> 19:48.950
And a broom.

19:49.000 --> 19:49.950
The girls say...

19:50.000 --> 19:53.950
Abigail Cross's dress and boots are in the bedroom.

19:54.000 --> 19:56.950
Someone wants to scare us. Says Bill.

19:57.000 --> 19:58.950
The door of the house is always open.

19:59.000 --> 20:00.950
Anyone can enter.

20:01.000 --> 20:02.950
This is a very old house.

20:03.000 --> 20:05.950
Old houses have old clothes.

20:06.000 --> 20:08.950
Nick is very quiet.

20:09.000 --> 20:09.950
Then he says...

20:10.000 --> 20:11.950
This is exciting.

20:12.000 --> 20:14.950
On Monday we can tell our friends about this place.

20:15.000 --> 20:16.950
Maybe we can see a ghost.

20:17.000 --> 20:18.950
Ghosts.

20:19.000 --> 20:19.950
House Silly.

20:20.000 --> 20:20.950
Come on.

20:21.000 --> 20:23.950
Let's start cleaning. Says Bill.

20:24.000 --> 20:26.950
They clean the windows, the table and the chairs.

20:27.000 --> 20:28.950
It's 5 p.m.

20:29.000 --> 20:30.950
It's time to go home. Says Nick.

20:31.000 --> 20:32.950
I help my parents at the restaurant.

20:33.000 --> 20:35.950
The restaurant is always full on Saturdays.

20:36.000 --> 20:38.950
We can return tomorrow for the decorations.

20:39.000 --> 20:43.950
We must also talk about the games for the party. Says Susan.

20:44.000 --> 20:44.950
Okay.

20:45.000 --> 20:48.950
Let's meet here tomorrow at 1 p.m. Says Bill.

20:49.000 --> 20:50.950
Everyone goes home.

20:51.000 --> 20:55.950
After dinner, Mrs. Connor makes Halloween cookies and pumpkin pies.

20:56.000 --> 20:59.950
Mr. Connor puts the jack-o-lantern in front of the window.

21:00.000 --> 21:02.950
Kelly and Megan go to their room.

21:03.000 --> 21:05.950
They want to make their Halloween costumes.

21:06.000 --> 21:10.950
Do you think Abigail Cross is a ghost? Asks Kelly.

21:11.000 --> 21:12.950
I'm very confused.

21:13.000 --> 21:16.950
I don't know, but that house is evil.

21:17.000 --> 21:19.950
I don't want to be afraid. Says Kelly.

21:20.000 --> 21:22.950
I want to have fun at the Halloween party.

21:23.000 --> 21:23.950
You're right.

21:24.000 --> 21:26.950
Let's not talk about ghosts. Says Megan.

21:27.000 --> 21:29.950
The girls start making their Halloween costumes.

21:30.000 --> 21:32.950
I want to be an alien. Says Megan.

21:33.000 --> 21:34.950
Look at my green mask.

21:35.000 --> 21:35.950
It's nice.

21:36.000 --> 21:36.950
I like it.

21:37.000 --> 21:38.950
But what can I be?

21:39.000 --> 21:40.950
Kelly thinks for a long time.

21:41.000 --> 21:42.950
Then she says...

21:43.000 --> 21:45.950
I want to be Abigail Cross, the witch.

21:46.000 --> 21:46.950
No, Kelly.

21:47.000 --> 21:48.950
Don't do it. Says Megan.

21:49.000 --> 21:49.950
Why not?

21:50.000 --> 21:51.950
It's an easy costume.

21:52.000 --> 21:54.950
I can wear mom's long black dress.

21:55.000 --> 21:56.950
Then I can buy a mask and a wig.

21:57.000 --> 21:58.950
I have a pair of old black boots.

21:59.000 --> 22:00.950
I want to scare everyone.

22:01.000 --> 22:01.950
Kelly laughs.

22:02.000 --> 22:04.950
Aren't you afraid? Asks Megan.

22:05.000 --> 22:08.950
No, it's just a Halloween costume. Says Kelly.

22:09.000 --> 22:10.950
Remember, our costumes are a secret.

22:11.000 --> 22:12.950
Don't tell anyone.

22:13.000 --> 22:18.950
On Sunday afternoon, the five friends meet at the abandoned house.

22:19.000 --> 22:21.950
When they enter, they look at the portrait.

22:22.000 --> 22:24.950
The woman has the same evil smile.

22:25.000 --> 22:28.950
But there is something different in the portrait.

22:29.000 --> 22:30.950
Megan sees it.

22:31.000 --> 22:32.950
She turns on her torch and says...

22:33.000 --> 22:35.950
Look at the woman in the portrait.

22:36.000 --> 22:38.950
She has a red mark around her neck.

22:39.000 --> 22:40.950
You're right. Says Nick.

22:41.000 --> 22:42.950
They all look at the portrait.

22:43.000 --> 22:44.950
What does it mean?

22:45.000 --> 22:46.950
It's your imagination, says Bill.

22:47.000 --> 22:49.950
You can see the red mark because you have a torch.

22:50.000 --> 22:54.950
Who wants to go downstairs and see the basement? Asks Bill.

22:55.000 --> 22:57.950
We can use the basement for scary games.

22:58.000 --> 23:00.950
You boys can go to the basement. Says Susan.

23:01.000 --> 23:04.950
We want to move the old tables to the center of the room.

23:05.000 --> 23:07.950
Megan goes to the dark bedroom.

23:08.000 --> 23:13.000
She opens the door and looks inside.

23:14.000 --> 23:18.950
The black dress and the black boots are still there.

23:19.000 --> 23:20.950
She shuts the door quickly.

23:21.000 --> 23:23.950
Her heart is beating fast.

23:24.000 --> 23:25.950
When the boys return, they say...

23:26.000 --> 23:27.950
There is nothing in the basement.

23:28.000 --> 23:31.000
Only some old barrels.

23:37.000 --> 23:40.950
Megan, Kelly, and Susan go back to the big room.

23:41.000 --> 23:43.950
They look at the old portrait.

23:44.000 --> 23:45.950
They don't like it.

23:46.000 --> 23:50.950
Soon the boys arrive with some cleaning products and a broom.

23:51.000 --> 23:52.950
The girls say...

23:53.000 --> 23:56.950
Abigail crosses dress and boots are in the bedroom.

23:57.000 --> 23:59.950
Someone wants to scare us. Says Bill.

24:00.000 --> 24:02.950
The door of the house is always open.

24:03.000 --> 24:04.950
Anyone can enter.

24:05.000 --> 24:07.950
This is a very old house.

24:08.000 --> 24:10.950
Old houses have old clothes.

24:11.000 --> 24:12.950
Nick is very quiet.

24:13.000 --> 24:14.950
Then he says...

24:15.000 --> 24:16.950
This is exciting.

24:17.000 --> 24:19.950
On Monday we can tell our friends about this place.

24:20.000 --> 24:22.950
Maybe we can see a ghost.

24:23.000 --> 24:27.000
Now turn to page 34 and check.

24:33.000 --> 24:34.950
Salem Halloween Cookies.

24:35.000 --> 24:38.950
It's fun to organize a Halloween party in your home.

24:39.000 --> 24:40.950
It's easy too.

24:41.000 --> 24:43.950
First, find a big room you can use.

24:44.000 --> 24:46.950
Second, make some scary decorations.

24:47.000 --> 24:49.950
Third, prepare some Halloween food.

24:50.000 --> 24:57.950
Popcorn, apples, sweets, pumpkin pies, and special Halloween cookies.

24:58.000 --> 25:00.950
Make Salem Halloween cookies for your party.

25:01.000 --> 25:01.950
It's easy.

25:02.000 --> 25:03.950
Just follow the recipe.

25:04.000 --> 25:05.950
Ingredients.

25:06.000 --> 25:09.950
Three-quarters of a cup of chopped nuts.

25:10.000 --> 25:12.950
One cup softened butter.

25:13.000 --> 25:15.950
Half a cup of powdered sugar.

25:16.000 --> 25:17.950
Half a cup flour.

25:18.000 --> 25:20.950
One teaspoon vanilla extract.

25:21.000 --> 25:23.950
Quarter of a teaspoon salt.

25:24.000 --> 25:25.950
Powdered sugar.

25:26.000 --> 25:27.950
Utensils to use.

25:28.000 --> 25:29.950
A big bowl.

25:30.000 --> 25:30.950
A wooden spoon.

25:31.000 --> 25:32.950
A teaspoon.

25:33.000 --> 25:34.950
A nonstick cookie sheet.

25:35.000 --> 25:38.950
Now chop the nuts.

25:39.000 --> 25:43.950
Mix together nuts, butter, sugar, and vanilla in the bowl.

25:44.000 --> 25:47.950
Slowly add flour and salt.

25:48.000 --> 25:51.950
Put the bowl in the refrigerator for one hour.

25:52.000 --> 25:53.950
Then make little balls.

25:54.000 --> 25:58.950
About two and a half centimeters in diameter.

25:59.000 --> 26:02.950
Roll each ball in powdered sugar three times.

26:03.000 --> 26:04.950
Put the balls on a cookie sheet.

26:05.000 --> 26:06.950
Bake in the oven,

26:07.000 --> 26:11.950
175 degrees Celsius, for 30 minutes.

26:12.000 --> 26:14.000
Happy Halloween.

26:19.000 --> 26:20.950
Chapter 6.

26:21.000 --> 26:23.950
Mysterious names.

26:24.000 --> 26:26.950
The girls look at the floor.

26:27.000 --> 26:28.950
This floor is very dirty.

26:29.000 --> 26:32.950
It is made of stone and it's difficult to clean.

26:33.000 --> 26:37.950
Let's wash it with hot water and detergent. Says Susan.

26:38.000 --> 26:44.950
So Susan and Kelly wash the stone floor.

26:45.000 --> 26:47.950
Suddenly Susan stops washing.

26:48.000 --> 26:51.950
She looks at the stones and says...

26:52.000 --> 26:53.950
I can't believe this.

26:54.000 --> 26:56.950
There are names on these stones.

26:57.000 --> 26:58.950
Her friends come and look.

26:59.000 --> 27:02.950
One name is George Johnson.

27:03.000 --> 27:06.950
Then there's Rebecca Putnam and Sarah Morley.

27:07.000 --> 27:09.950
This is very strange, says Bill.

27:10.000 --> 27:11.950
Look at the other names.

27:12.000 --> 27:14.950
He reads them and then he counts them.

27:15.000 --> 27:16.950
There are twenty.

27:17.000 --> 27:18.950
This is a mystery.

27:19.000 --> 27:20.950
Who wrote them?

27:21.000 --> 27:22.950
What do they mean?

27:23.000 --> 27:24.950
Can you repeat the names?

27:25.000 --> 27:28.950
Perhaps I can find them in my book. Says Susan.

27:29.000 --> 27:30.950
Bill tells her the names.

27:31.000 --> 27:33.950
She finds all of them in her book.

27:34.000 --> 27:35.950
How spooky.

27:36.000 --> 27:40.950
These are the names of the twenty witches of the hangings of 1692.

27:41.000 --> 27:44.950
There are seven men and thirteen women.

27:45.000 --> 27:46.950
Look at this page.

27:47.000 --> 27:51.950
The Salem witch hangings of 1692.

27:52.000 --> 27:53.950
June 10th.

27:54.000 --> 27:55.950
One hanging.

27:56.000 --> 27:57.950
July 19th.

27:58.000 --> 27:59.950
Five hangings.

28:00.000 --> 28:01.950
August 19th.

28:02.000 --> 28:03.950
Five hangings.

28:04.000 --> 28:05.950
September 19th.

28:06.000 --> 28:06.950
One hanging.

28:07.000 --> 28:09.950
September 22nd.

28:10.000 --> 28:11.950
Eight hangings.

28:12.000 --> 28:13.950
What can we do? Asks Kelly.

28:14.000 --> 28:15.950
Nothing says Bill.

28:16.000 --> 28:18.950
Are you afraid of names on stones?

28:19.000 --> 28:21.950
These are not the names of ordinary people.

28:22.000 --> 28:25.950
These are the names of twenty witches. Says Megan.

28:26.000 --> 28:28.950
Witches have magic powers.

28:29.000 --> 28:30.950
We can show our friends at the party.

28:31.000 --> 28:34.950
We can scare them. Says Nick laughing.

28:35.000 --> 28:36.950
That's a great idea.

28:37.000 --> 28:39.950
This Halloween party is exciting. Says Bill.

28:40.000 --> 28:42.950
Let's put the decorations on the walls.

28:43.000 --> 28:45.950
There are bats, spiders, and pumpkins.

28:46.000 --> 28:49.950
Who wants to bring the food and drinks? Asks Nick.

28:50.000 --> 28:54.950
Megan and I can bring pumpkin pies and Halloween cookies. Says Kelly.

28:55.000 --> 28:58.950
I can bring apple pies, popcorn, and sweets. Says Susan.

28:59.000 --> 29:03.950
Let me bring drinks and candles. Says Bill.

29:04.000 --> 29:07.950
Then I can bring paper plates, paper cups, and a paper table cloth.

29:08.000 --> 29:10.950
I can also bring some chairs. Says Nick.

29:11.000 --> 29:13.950
Don't forget your portable radio, Nick. Says Kelly.

29:14.000 --> 29:14.950
Okay.

29:15.000 --> 29:17.950
So everything is ready for the party, says Bill.

29:18.000 --> 29:20.950
We must be here at eight o'clock to prepare things.

29:21.000 --> 29:24.950
The party starts at nine p.m.

29:25.000 --> 29:30.950
It's Monday, October 31st, Halloween.

29:31.000 --> 29:36.950
There are Halloween decorations in the homes, in the shops, and in the classrooms.

29:37.000 --> 29:43.950
When school finishes, Kelly buys a wig and a mask of an old lady.

29:44.000 --> 29:47.950
That evening, Kelly and Megan put on their costumes.

29:48.000 --> 29:50.950
When Mrs. Connor sees them, she says.

29:51.000 --> 29:52.950
What wonderful costumes.

29:53.000 --> 29:56.950
A green alien and an old lady.

29:57.000 --> 29:59.950
I'm not an ordinary old lady.

30:00.000 --> 30:04.950
I'm a Salem witch, and the year is 1692. Says Kelly.

30:05.000 --> 30:06.950
Wow. Says Mr. Connor.

30:07.000 --> 30:08.950
Where is the party?

30:09.000 --> 30:12.950
It's at the abandoned house near the old cemetery.

30:13.000 --> 30:14.950
That's exciting.

30:15.000 --> 30:16.950
Have fun. Says Mr. Connor.

30:17.000 --> 30:18.950
Goodbye, girls.

30:19.000 --> 30:26.950
Have fun. Says Mrs. Connor.

30:27.000 --> 30:28.950
Chapter seven.

30:29.000 --> 30:35.950
The House of Horrors.

30:36.000 --> 30:39.950
The five friends meet at eight that evening.

30:40.000 --> 30:42.950
Everyone has a scary costume.

30:43.000 --> 30:44.950
Bill is a vampire.

30:45.000 --> 30:46.950
Nick is a skeleton.

30:47.000 --> 30:49.950
Susan is a ghost.

30:50.000 --> 30:53.950
When they see Kelly's costume, they laugh and say.

30:54.000 --> 30:58.950
Good evening Mrs. Abigail Ross.

30:59.000 --> 31:02.950
They cover the old table with a paper table cloth.

31:03.000 --> 31:06.950
Then they put the food and drinks on the table.

31:07.000 --> 31:16.950
They light the candles because there is no electricity.

31:17.000 --> 31:19.950
Nick turns on his portable radio.

31:20.000 --> 31:22.950
Meghan goes to the dark bedroom.

31:23.000 --> 31:26.950
She opens the door and looks inside.

31:27.000 --> 31:32.950
The black dress and black boots are not there.

31:33.000 --> 31:36.950
She is afraid, but she says nothing to her friends.

31:37.000 --> 31:38.950
Soon their friends arrive.

31:39.000 --> 31:42.950
They all have scary costumes and masks.

31:43.000 --> 31:45.950
Is this a haunted house?

31:46.000 --> 31:47.950
It's very spooky.

31:48.000 --> 31:50.950
They say no one answers.

31:51.000 --> 31:53.950
Some boys and girls dance.

31:54.000 --> 31:56.950
Others eat, talk, and laugh.

31:57.000 --> 31:58.950
Several hours pass.

31:59.000 --> 32:01.000
Everyone is happy.

32:02.000 --> 32:03.950
It's a great party.

32:04.000 --> 32:06.950
They say.

32:07.000 --> 32:12.950
It's time for the treasure hunt. Says Bill, you all have different maps.

32:13.000 --> 32:15.950
Let's start.

32:16.000 --> 32:18.950
Everyone starts in a different room.

32:19.000 --> 32:20.950
Some start in the kitchen.

32:21.000 --> 32:23.950
Others start in the bedrooms.

32:24.000 --> 32:28.950
Kelly takes her torch and goes downstairs to the basement.

32:29.000 --> 32:32.950
She looks inside a big barrel.

32:33.000 --> 32:34.950
It is very dark.

32:35.000 --> 32:38.950
And Kelly is in the basement alone.

32:39.000 --> 32:43.950
Suddenly there is a sweet smell of roses.

32:44.000 --> 32:47.950
She turns on her torch and she is terrified.

32:48.000 --> 32:51.950
The old lady from the museum is standing by the barrel.

32:52.000 --> 32:54.950
You are not Abigail Cross.

32:55.000 --> 32:57.950
I am Abigail Cross.

32:58.000 --> 33:01.950
Tonight is Halloween and you are in my house.

33:02.000 --> 33:05.950
On this night we spirits look for young bodies.

33:06.000 --> 33:09.950
When we find a young body we can live again.

33:10.000 --> 33:13.950
At midnight my spirit enters your body.

33:14.000 --> 33:17.950
You must die so that I can live.

33:18.000 --> 33:20.950
Kelly's heart is beating fast.

33:21.000 --> 33:23.950
Her legs can't move.

33:24.000 --> 33:25.950
She has no voice.

33:26.000 --> 33:30.950
Abigail Cross touches Kelly with her cold hand.

33:31.000 --> 33:34.950
She takes off Kelly's mask and wig.

33:35.000 --> 33:37.950
Your bed is in the barrel.

33:38.000 --> 33:39.950
You are tired.

33:40.000 --> 33:42.950
You must sleep forever.

33:43.000 --> 33:44.950
Kelly obeys.

33:45.000 --> 33:47.950
She goes to sleep inside the barrel.

33:48.000 --> 33:52.950
Abigail puts on Kelly's mask and wig.

33:53.000 --> 33:56.000
She goes upstairs to the party.

34:02.000 --> 34:04.950
At half past 11 Nick says...

34:05.000 --> 34:06.950
It's almost midnight.

34:07.000 --> 34:09.950
Let's sit down and take off our masks.

34:10.000 --> 34:12.950
We want to see the person behind the mask.

34:13.000 --> 34:14.950
Nick asks...

34:15.000 --> 34:16.950
Who is the alien?

34:17.000 --> 34:18.950
The alien takes off her mask.

34:19.000 --> 34:20.950
It's Megan!

34:21.000 --> 34:22.950
Everyone laughs.

34:23.000 --> 34:24.950
And who is the ghost?

34:25.000 --> 34:27.950
It's Susan!

34:28.000 --> 34:31.950
Who is the old lady? asks Bill.

34:32.000 --> 34:34.950
The old lady takes off her mask.

34:35.000 --> 34:36.950
Everyone screams.

34:37.000 --> 34:39.950
It's Abigail Cross's ghost.

34:40.000 --> 34:42.950
Her face is white and her eyes are red.

34:43.000 --> 34:45.950
She has a red mark around her neck.

34:46.000 --> 34:49.950
She laughs and her teeth are black.

34:50.000 --> 34:51.950
Everyone is terrified.

34:52.000 --> 34:53.950
Bill looks at her and says...

34:54.000 --> 34:55.950
That's Kelly's costume.

34:56.000 --> 34:56.950
Where is Kelly?

34:57.000 --> 34:58.950
I am Kelly.

34:59.000 --> 35:02.950
At midnight my spirit enters her body.

35:03.000 --> 35:04.950
Remember, I am a witch.

35:05.000 --> 35:07.950
Everyone wants to run away.

35:08.000 --> 35:11.950
They go to the door, but they cannot open it.

35:12.000 --> 35:16.950
There are the horrible faces of the other ghosts outside the windows.

35:17.000 --> 35:19.950
The ghosts are looking inside.

35:20.000 --> 35:22.950
Who are these people? asks Bill.

35:23.000 --> 35:28.950
They are the witches of the hangings of 1692.

35:29.000 --> 35:31.950
Look at the red mark on my neck.

35:32.000 --> 35:34.950
This is the mark of the rope.

35:35.000 --> 35:39.950
20 witches for 20 young bodies.

35:40.000 --> 35:42.950
Now you are in my house.

35:43.000 --> 35:46.950
This is the house of horrors.

35:47.000 --> 35:50.950
No one leaves this house alive.

35:51.000 --> 35:54.950
At midnight our spirits enter your bodies.

35:55.000 --> 35:56.950
We want to live again.

35:57.000 --> 36:01.950
We want to bring evil to Salem. Says Abigail Cross.

36:02.000 --> 36:03.950
Where is Kelly? asks Bill.

36:04.000 --> 36:06.950
Look at the portrait on the wall.

36:07.000 --> 36:08.950
laughs the witch.

36:09.000 --> 36:11.950
Everyone looks at the portrait.

36:12.000 --> 36:14.950
They see Kelly's face.

36:15.000 --> 36:16.950
Her lips are red.

36:17.000 --> 36:19.950
And there is a red mark around her neck.

36:20.000 --> 36:26.000
This is our party, not yours. Screams the witch.

36:32.000 --> 36:35.950
They meet at the old house.

36:36.000 --> 36:39.950
Everyone is wearing scary costumes.

36:40.000 --> 36:42.950
The boys light candles.

36:43.000 --> 36:46.950
Everyone is ready for the party.

36:47.000 --> 36:52.950
Megan goes to the bedroom, but she sees nobody there.

36:53.000 --> 36:55.950
Soon their friends arrive.

36:56.000 --> 36:57.950
The party starts.

36:58.000 --> 37:00.950
Everyone is happy.

37:01.000 --> 37:03.950
Then there is a treasure hunt.

37:04.000 --> 37:10.000
Kelly goes downstairs and looks inside a big barrel.

37:15.000 --> 37:16.950
Chapter 8.

37:17.000 --> 37:19.950
Fire.

37:20.000 --> 37:24.950
Suddenly the decorations on the wall start moving.

37:25.000 --> 37:27.950
The bats are flying around the room.

37:28.000 --> 37:32.950
They are making strange noises. Screams a girl.

37:33.000 --> 37:36.950
There is a bat in my hair. Screams a boy.

37:37.000 --> 37:38.950
This bat is a vampire.

37:39.000 --> 37:41.950
Slowly the ghosts enter the house.

37:42.000 --> 37:44.950
They penetrate the walls.

37:45.000 --> 37:47.950
They are really spooky.

37:48.000 --> 37:50.950
They move around their victims.

37:51.000 --> 37:53.950
Megan and Susan are terrified and say...

37:54.000 --> 37:55.950
They are waiting for midnight.

37:56.000 --> 37:58.950
Do you remember the 20 names on the floor?

37:59.000 --> 38:01.950
These are their ghosts.

38:02.000 --> 38:04.950
We must find Kelly. Says Megan.

38:05.000 --> 38:07.950
A candle on the table falls.

38:08.000 --> 38:12.950
The paper tablecloth is burning.

38:13.000 --> 38:13.950
Fire.

38:14.000 --> 38:16.950
We must get out of here. Says Bill.

38:17.000 --> 38:19.950
Oh no, it's a big fire. Says Susan.

38:20.000 --> 38:22.950
We can't open the door. Says Nick.

38:23.000 --> 38:23.950
It's five to midnight.

38:24.000 --> 38:26.950
At midnight the ghosts take our bodies.

38:27.000 --> 38:27.950
What can we do?

38:28.000 --> 38:30.950
I must find Kelly. Says Bill.

38:31.000 --> 38:34.950
He takes his torch and runs to the basement.

38:35.000 --> 38:36.950
He looks in all the barrels.

38:37.000 --> 38:39.950
Finally, he sees Kelly.

38:40.000 --> 38:40.950
She is sleeping.

38:41.000 --> 38:43.950
Kelly! Kelly! Says Bill.

38:44.000 --> 38:45.950
Wake up! Wake up!

38:46.000 --> 38:47.950
Kelly does not wake up.

38:48.000 --> 38:50.950
Kelly! Says Bill. Kelly!

38:51.000 --> 38:56.950
Bill takes Kelly in his arms and carries her upstairs.

38:57.000 --> 38:59.950
It's two minutes to midnight.

39:00.000 --> 39:01.950
There is fire everywhere.

39:02.000 --> 39:04.950
The room is full of black smoke.

39:05.000 --> 39:07.950
Everyone is terrified.

39:08.000 --> 39:10.950
Bats and spiders are flying in the air.

39:11.000 --> 39:14.950
The ghosts are waiting for midnight.

39:15.000 --> 39:18.000
No one can open the door or the windows.

39:19.000 --> 39:21.950
Suddenly, the portrait is burning.

39:22.000 --> 39:25.950
The fire is destroying the evil spirit.

39:26.000 --> 39:27.950
Look! Exclaims Megan.

39:28.000 --> 39:29.950
Abigail Cross is burning.

39:30.000 --> 39:31.950
Yes! Says Nick.

39:32.000 --> 39:33.950
And the other ghosts are burning too.

39:34.000 --> 39:36.950
Look! The door is opening. Says Bill.

39:37.000 --> 39:38.950
Quick! Let's go!

39:39.000 --> 39:41.950
Everyone runs outside.

39:42.000 --> 39:44.000
Bill carries.

39:45.000 --> 39:46.950
Everyone runs outside.

39:47.000 --> 39:48.950
Bill carries Kelly outside.

39:49.000 --> 39:52.950
Is everyone here? Asks Nick. He counts.

39:53.000 --> 39:55.950
There are twenty people.

39:56.000 --> 40:00.950
The fire destroys the house and the evil ghosts inside.

40:01.000 --> 40:03.950
Terrible noises come from the house.

40:04.000 --> 40:10.000
This is the scariest Halloween party of my life. Says one of the boys.

40:11.000 --> 40:13.950
Megan and Bill are waking up Kelly.

40:14.000 --> 40:15.950
She is still sleeping.

40:16.000 --> 40:17.950
But no one can wake her up.

40:18.000 --> 40:20.950
Is she in a coma? Asks Megan.

40:21.000 --> 40:23.950
I don't know! Answers Bill.

40:24.000 --> 40:25.950
Everyone is standing near Kelly.

40:26.000 --> 40:29.950
Oh Kelly, please wake up. Says Megan.

40:30.000 --> 40:31.950
Suddenly, it starts raining.

40:32.000 --> 40:34.950
There is thunder and lightning.

40:35.000 --> 40:36.950
Kelly moves her head.

40:37.000 --> 40:37.950
Where am I?

40:38.000 --> 40:38.950
She asks.

40:39.000 --> 40:43.950
Oh Kelly, you're okay. I'm so happy. Says Megan.

40:44.000 --> 40:47.950
What's happening? Asks Kelly.

40:48.000 --> 40:51.950
Bill smiles and explains everything to her.

40:52.000 --> 40:55.950
Do you believe in ghosts now? Asks Nick.

40:56.000 --> 40:57.950
Bill looks at him.

40:58.000 --> 40:59.950
And slowly says...

41:00.000 --> 41:01.950
Well...

41:02.000 --> 41:04.000
Yes.

41:09.000 --> 41:11.950
Then they all go home.

41:12.000 --> 41:15.950
Kelly has some strange dreams that night.

41:16.000 --> 41:18.950
The next morning she wakes up early.

41:19.000 --> 41:20.950
Megan is still sleeping.

41:21.000 --> 41:23.950
She is happy to be home.

41:24.000 --> 41:26.950
She gets up and goes to the bathroom.

41:27.000 --> 41:31.950
She looks in the mirror and cannot believe her eyes.

41:32.000 --> 41:33.950
What can she see?

41:34.000 --> 41:36.950
A red mark around her neck.

41:37.000 --> 41:39.950
A mysterious voice in the mirror says...

41:40.000 --> 41:45.000
When you play with fire, Kelly, you burn your fingers.

41:52.000 --> 41:55.950
Suddenly, the decorations on the wall start moving.

41:56.000 --> 41:58.950
The bats are flying around the room.

41:59.000 --> 42:01.950
They are making strange noises.

42:02.000 --> 42:03.950
No! Screams a girl.

42:04.000 --> 42:05.950
There's a bat in my hair!

42:06.000 --> 42:07.950
Help! Screams a boy.

42:08.000 --> 42:09.950
This bat is a vampire!

42:10.000 --> 42:13.950
Slowly, the ghosts enter the house.

42:14.000 --> 42:16.950
They penetrate the walls.

42:17.000 --> 42:19.950
They are really spooky.

42:20.000 --> 42:22.950
They move around their victims.

42:23.000 --> 42:25.950
Megan and Susan are terrified and say...

42:26.000 --> 42:27.950
They're waiting for midnight.

42:28.000 --> 42:30.950
Do you remember the twenty names on the floor?

42:31.000 --> 42:32.950
These are their ghosts.

42:33.000 --> 42:34.950
We must find Kelly.

42:35.000 --> 42:36.950
It says Megan.

42:37.000 --> 42:39.950
A candle on the table falls.

42:40.000 --> 42:42.950
The paper table cloth is burning.

42:43.000 --> 42:43.950
Fire!

42:44.000 --> 42:44.950
We must get out of here.

42:45.000 --> 42:46.950
It says Bill.

42:47.000 --> 42:48.950
Oh no, it's a big fire.

42:49.000 --> 42:50.950
It says Susan.

42:51.000 --> 42:51.950
We can't open the door.

42:52.000 --> 42:52.950
It says Nick.

42:53.000 --> 42:53.950
It's five to midnight.

42:54.000 --> 42:56.950
At midnight, the ghosts take our bodies.

42:57.000 --> 42:58.950
What can we do?

42:59.000 --> 43:00.950
I must find Kelly.

43:01.000 --> 43:02.950
It says Bill.

43:03.000 --> 43:05.950
It says Torch and runs to the basement.

43:06.000 --> 43:07.950
He looks in all the barrels.

43:08.000 --> 43:10.950
Finally, he sees Kelly.

43:11.000 --> 43:13.000
She is sleeping.

43:18.000 --> 43:19.950
Make a bat.

43:20.000 --> 43:21.950
You need...

43:22.000 --> 43:23.950
A square piece of paper.

43:24.000 --> 43:27.950
Colored on one side and white on the other side.

43:28.000 --> 43:30.950
A pair of scissors.

43:31.000 --> 43:32.950
One.

43:33.000 --> 43:36.950
Fold the square in half from top to bottom.

43:37.000 --> 43:38.950
Two.

43:39.000 --> 43:43.950
Fold and unfold in half from side to side.

43:44.000 --> 43:45.950
Three.

43:46.000 --> 43:48.950
Fold one half up along the middle fold line.

43:49.000 --> 43:52.950
Start to open out the paper.

43:53.000 --> 43:53.950
Four.

43:54.000 --> 43:58.950
And with your free hand, press it down.

43:59.000 --> 44:00.950
Five.

44:01.000 --> 44:04.950
Neatly into a triangle.

44:05.000 --> 44:05.950
Six.

44:06.000 --> 44:07.950
Turn the paper over.

44:08.000 --> 44:11.950
Repeat steps two to five.

44:12.000 --> 44:13.950
Seven.

44:14.000 --> 44:17.950
Fold one of the right hand corners to the middle fold line.

44:18.000 --> 44:21.950
Do the same with the other left hand corner.

44:22.000 --> 44:23.950
Eight.

44:24.000 --> 44:27.950
Fold the right bottom corners in to make the bat's feet.

44:28.000 --> 44:31.950
Nine.

44:32.000 --> 44:34.950
Carefully cut the paper as shown.

44:35.000 --> 44:41.950
Fold the top point down so making the bat's head and ears appear.

44:42.000 --> 44:42.950
Ten.

44:43.000 --> 44:48.950
To complete the bat, fold the tips of its feet out towards you.

44:49.000 --> 44:54.000
Don't forget to draw the eyes and fangs!
